      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-02-01_WidnesExaminer_art0010" n="art0010">
        <head>2 FOR DEUS CALCSIOu SE McDOUGALL'S SELF RAISING FLOUR</head>
        <p>2 FOR DEUS CALCSIOu SE McDOUGALL'S SELF RAISING FLOUR</p>
        <p>TH KI YS</p>
        <p>Where They Are and What. They Do</p>
        <p>Everyone ought to know how to tell whether the kidneys are acting properly, for their work is of great importance—" you cautiot be well if your kidneys are ill."</p>
        <p>What The Kidneys Are and What They DO.----The kidneys are two bean-shaped organs lying beneath the small of the back (see ilrustration). They are composed of thousands or little filtering tubes through which the blood flows hundred of times a day to be filtered.</p>
        <p>Enough poisonous waste gets into the blood every leic clays to cause death. Your kidneys alone can sare you. Erery .?4• hours they take out about 500 grains of poisonous waste and pints of water from the blood.</p>
        <p>What Happens when the Kidneys are Weak.—The kidneys are s'.) delicate that the least cold, chill, ,train, or excess may affect them. Then they are likely to leave some of the poisonous kidney waste in the blood. This poisonous waste gets carried to all parts of the body ; makes you feel cull, heavy and irritable makes your back ache, your limbs ache and swell you may become rheumatic or dropsical, or suffer with the sharp pains of lumbago.</p>
        <p>Kidney poison shows itself in the water, which may be cloudy or sandy. There may be pain in seeking relief, or you may be disturbed several times HI the night. The urinary channels may become clogged up with gravel, or stones may form in the kidneys and bladder.</p>
        <p>Weiner), and even children, as well as men, are subject to kidney and bladder disorders.</p>
        <p>Treatment—Patient should drink plenty of water to keep the urine dilute, and should take nothing that may excite the kidneys. A dose of Doan's Backache Kidney Pills after each meal, and before retiring at night, will help to clear the offending deposits from the kidneys and urinary system. This remedy is compounded from ingredients of the highest quality and absolute purity. It acts on the kidneys and bladder only, an,?:l is not intended for constipation or disorders of the digestive system.</p>
        <p>matter, said "If you do as I tell you, you'll get off those sticks in a very short time.) " ; her advice was to try Doan's backache kidney pills, so my son sent for a box. I had not taken many doses of these before I could do without the sticks, and within a week I started work again: since then I've never had any trouble with my back. (Signed) " JosENI PrticE." Yearly 4 years later, Mr. Price said :—" I am pleased to say I have never had any return of the pains since I used Doan's pills.</p>
        <p>Price 2;9 a box, six boxes 13/9; of all chemists and stores, or front Foster-McClellan. Co., 8, Wells-st., Oxford-st., London, W. Don't ask for backache or kidney pills—ask for DOAN'S Backache Kidney Pills, the same as Mr. Price had.</p>
