        <p>MYSTERY PLAY NOT TO BE ACTED IN CHURCH. Almost at the last moment the Bishop of London has intervened and prohibited the performance of a Mystery Play in the Church of St. Silas-the-Martyr, Kentish Town. The Bishop considers it to be undesirable that plays should be acted in church.</p>
        <p>BURGLARS UP A TREE. Awakened at 4 o'clock on Thursday morning by a barking dog, Mr James Gibb, of 290, Finchley-road London, came down to find his dining-room ransacked and a window open. Silver articles were scattered about the floor and others, to the value of £2OO, bad been stolen. He sent for the police and got his son to drive his motor-car quickly round and round the block in which the house was situated. The block was sur- rounded in the fog by police, and eventually two young men named Jones and Harrison were found up a tree in one of the gardens. In their possession, it was stated, was a large part of the stolen articles and an unloaded revolver.</p>
